# Elix keys. Copy this file to .env and fill in the values:
#
#     copy .env.example .env        (Windows CMD)
#     cp .env.example .env          (PowerShell / bash)
#
# .env is gitignored, so your keys are never committed.
#
# Cloud and local providers. Elix picks the first available model from the
# config/models.yaml preference lists, in the vision's order:
#   groq   -> https://api.groq.com/openai/v1      (chat, planning, STT, TTS, guard)
#   nvidia -> https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 (chat fallback; a 402 opens a 24h breaker)
#   hf     -> https://router.huggingface.co/v1   (chat fallback, embeddings)
#   ollama -> http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1          (local; NO key, silently absent if not running)
#
# The `builtin` provider needs no key: it is Elix's own scripted fallback code.
#
# If every provider is down or out of quota, Elix says "brb, lag" and keeps
# playing on reflex + skill code. Nothing here is required for `elix start` —
# without keys, phase 2 still connects and plays, and every reply comes from
# the scripted pool.
# NVIDIA (the middle tier in the vision: Groq -> NVIDIA -> Hugging Face -> local).
# Free credits are limited; a 402 here opens the provider's breaker for 24 hours.
# NEVER COMMIT THIS FILE. If a key is ever shared or pasted, rotate it.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

GROQ_API_KEY=
HF_TOKEN=
